I think the EISA version was called KZESC. It's not bad either. I've got
one in an AS1000. Btw: I have seen a great performance improvement by
expanding the Mylex cache from 4 to 16MB and by using some RAID 1+0 instead
of RAID5. I certainly can't recommend RAID5 on those old Mylex controllers.

> I haven't tried incantations of disklabel because the command is
> entirely new to me. Which probably tells you that I'm *not* a unix
> guru, right ;-)
> But I understand your advice and will investigate.

I would first check kernel messages. When you create the disklabel
manually, a serial console is helpful. Disklabel calls an editor to let you
edit the disklabel. It's much easier if you first set TERM=vt100 and
EDITOR=vi. Unless of course you are one of those grey bearded Unix gurus
who like to edit files with ed. :-)

Dennis

