Yes, of course, I just thought that you weren't aware of the V5.1A 
complete documentation set which is online.

You are then getting aquainted with Tru64 then. Best of luck!

Have you tried to check the devices found from the command prompt when 
you booted from the O/S CD?
If you get to the command prompt and there check the devices e.g. by 
using scu as follows:

# scu show edt

What do you get?

Another way to do it would be:

# hwmgr show scsi

If the device called re0 (not DRA0 as in SRM or VMS) doesn't show up, it 
seems that there is a problem with the drivers. Booting from the 
installation CD should include all drivers for all supported hardware 
and therefore all supported devices should show up.

I used to support Tru64 at the local DEC/Compaq, but since the Tru64 was 
"killed", I haven't supported it for years anymore. Unfortunately I have 
forgotten many things and have to read manuals when there are some more 
exotic things happening.
Nowadays I'm doing VMS support for our customers (I'm not working for 
HP, but for a local IT company).

Kari



